={{ {
  model: 'llama3.1:8b-instruct-q4_K_M',
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'system',
      content: 'You are a classifier for a Solution Architecture pipeline. Analyze the user input and determine the mode, intent, and extract project information.\n\nMODE RULES:\n- mode=chat: For queries, help requests, status checks. Keywords: help, status, list, artifacts, jobs, what, how, show, get, query, ?\n- mode=execute: For creating/building/generating solution architecture. Keywords: build, create, generate, make, develop, design a, implement\n\nIf input is a single word like \"help\", \"list\", \"jobs\", \"status\" - it is ALWAYS mode=chat.\nIf input asks a question or requests information - it is mode=chat.\nOnly use mode=execute when user explicitly wants to CREATE or BUILD something new.\n\nPROJECT EXTRACTION:\n- Extract the project slug/name if mentioned (e.g., \"project healthcare-scheduler\" -> projectSlug: \"healthcare-scheduler\")\n- Look for patterns like: \"project X\", \"for X\", \"X project\"\n\nChat intents: help, status, artifacts, jobs, list\nExecute intents: create, build, generate\n\nOutput JSON only.'
    },
    { role: 'user', content: $json.rawInput || $json.requirements }
  ],
  stream: false,
  format: {
    type: 'object',
    required: ['mode', 'intent'],
    properties: {
      mode: { type: 'string', enum: ['chat', 'execute'] },
      intent: { type: 'string' },
      projectSlug: { type: 'string' },
      requirements: { type: 'string' }
    }
  },
  options: { temperature: 0.1 }
} }}

